    "## 12. Notes for the report\n",
    "* **Techniques**: LoRMA (exp1), partial FT (exp2), adapters (exp3), KD (exp4); compare `trainable_M`, `dev_macroF1_tuned`, `infer_docs_per_s` in the table.\n",
    "* **Ablations you can run cheaply** by editing one line and re-running with `FORCE_RERUN`: `select_chunks(..., strategy=\"head\" | \"uniform\" | \"smart\")` for the long-document study, `use_lwan=False` for the label-attention study, `loss` (`bce` vs `asl`), `alpha` rows in `cv_alpha` for per-label vs global thresholds.\n",
    "* Thresholds are tuned on dev only; no test information is used. LoRMA here is implemented as `W' = (I + BA)W` with identity-preserving initialisation; cite [12] and mention rank-inflation was not used."
